From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/32] Tests for the intermediate CA cache, index duplicates
 and session reuse

The three picks (cm-11 02e4d22, 5549787, 3f575a6 = conscrypt
04e7d1d, 4bdc877, 5af5e93) carry no tests upstream. These are tests
for their behaviour:

- TrustManagerImplTest.testLearnedIntermediateIsNotTrustAnchor
  (02e4d22): an intermediate CA with an IP name constraint (10/8) is
  learned from a valid chain; afterwards a leaf outside the constraint
  (192.168.0.1) is still rejected, with and without the intermediate in
  the presented chain, while a short chain inside it is still
  completed. Before 02e4d22 the learned intermediate became a trust
  anchor, whose own constraints PKIX does not apply;
- TrustManagerImplTest.testLearnedIntermediateCompletesChainToRoot
  (02e4d22): the assertions of testGetFullChain (a chain completed from
  the learned intermediate ends at the root) on a directly constructed
  TrustManagerImpl. testGetFullChain takes its trust manager from the
  default provider, which on host Dalvik is the jarjar'd
  com.android.org.conscrypt class, so its instanceof check fails there
  before the chains are compared;
- TrustedCertificateIndexTest (5549787): indexing one certificate many
  times stores it once; two different CAs with the same subject are
  both kept and each leaf finds its own issuer;
- NativeCryptoTest.test_SSL_session_reused (3f575a6): NULL throws, a
  new SSL and a full handshake report false, a resumed session reports
  true on both sides, and a session offered to a server that cannot
  resume it reports false;
- SSLSocketTest.test_SSLSocket_sessionReuse_onlyWhenResumed (3f575a6):
  with the same wrapped host and port, the client keeps its cached
  session object only when the server resumes it, and a server that
  cannot resume gets a new session that then replaces the cached one.

Android 4.2 port (android-4.2.2_r1) of patch 0018 of the 4.4 series,
made from its Android 4.3 port. Paths and names: libcore/crypto of 4.4
(org.conscrypt, org_conscrypt_NativeCrypto.cpp in libjavacrypto) is
libcore/luni on 4.2 (org.apache.harmony.xnet.provider.jsse,
org_apache_harmony_xnet_provider_jsse_NativeCrypto.cpp in libjavacore).
As on 4.3, NativeCryptoTest.handshake() has no ALPN parameter: the
session reuse test passes one null less. 4.2 handles are int: the
session reuse test keeps contexts, sessions and SSL pointers in int
variables and overrides the int Hooks methods. The 4.2 TestKeyStore
has no getRootCa() (added in 4.3 with the eKU change 90d02cb): it gets
the getRootCa() of 4.3, which returns the root CA its initCerts()
already builds, for the TrustManagerImplTest cases.
